.TH SESSLINT-HOOK 1 "" "SessLint 0.4.1" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-hook \- [read\-only] Agent hook entrypoint: reads one hook payload from stdin and checks the transcript.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint hook [\-\-event NAME] [\-\-init] [\-\-agent {claude,codex,all}] [\-f | \-\-format {text,json,claude\-json}] [\-\-json] [\-\-fail\-on {never,error,warning}] [\-\-profile PROFILE] [\-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}] [\-q | \-\-quiet] [\-v | \-\-verbose]
.SH DESCRIPTION
[read\-only] Reads one JSON hook payload from stdin (Claude Code contract: session_id, transcript_path, cwd, hook_event_name), resolves the transcript file, and runs the event\-appropriate integrity check. Prints one content\-free line and exits 0 (advisory) — or 1 when \-\-fail\-on gates on findings. Exit 2 is never emitted: hook checks never block the agent. \-\-init prints ready\-to\-merge hook snippets (never writes config).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-event NAME
Hook event name (e.g. SessionStart, PreCompact, PostCompact, SessionEnd). Unknown names run the generic integrity check.
.TP
.B \-\-init
Print ready\-to\-merge agent hook snippets (never writes config)
.TP
.B \-\-agent {claude,codex,all}
Agent to generate snippets for with \-\-init (default: all) Choices: claude, codex, all. Default: all.
.TP
.B \-f {text,json,claude\-json}, \-\-format {text,json,claude\-json}
Output format (default: text; claude\-json emits a content\-free systemMessage envelope) Choices: text, json, claude\-json.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON (shortcut for \-\-format json)
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on {never,error,warning}
Minimum finding severity that exits 1 (default: never — hook checks are advisory; 'warning' fails on any finding) Choices: never, error, warning.
.TP
.B \-\-profile PROFILE
Validation profile (default: neutral)
.TP
.B \-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}
Session format adapter (default: auto\-detect) Choices: auto, canonical, claude\-code\-jsonl, codex\-rollout, openai\-agents.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-error stderr output
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Print debug diagnostics (settings provenance, elapsed) to stderr
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — clean check, or repair executed, validated, and manifested.
.TP
.B 1
Finding / refusal — diagnostic errors found, repair plan blocked, or
execution refused (TOCTOU, SL203).
.TP
.B 2
Operational error — CLI syntax error, file not found, permission denied,
or live-DB path refusal.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1), sesslint\-completion(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

